"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Executor built /tmp/localrepo containing the sl .deb and a dpkg-scanpackages-generated Packages.gz, served it via python3 http.server bound to the node IP on port 8080, and directly confirmed the server responds with curl fetching Packages.gz (200/valid gzip content) both before and immediately after the install.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bcd4c09abe37425f\",\"cmd-e93fa5e5cf124655\",\"cmd-7fd420ce18ed4a2b\"]},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"Usual remote repositories are unreachable during the operation\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Remote mirrors (archive/security/ports/esm.ubuntu.com) were blackholed via /etc/hosts to 127.0.0.1; curl to archive.ubuntu.com returned connection-refused, and apt-get update showed explicit 'Could not connect' errors for all three remote hosts while the local repo (10.100.29.10:8080) fetched successfully in the same run, directly demonstrating the required unreachable-remote / reachable-local condition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0d46b3556f6c442f\",\"cmd-5f0748b37449452a\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"Install a package from the local repository while remote repos are unreachable\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"With remote mirrors still blackholed, apt-get install -y sl completed ('Need to get 0 B' since the deb was already local), and dpkg -l/-L plus apt-cache policy confirm sl 3.03-17build1 is installed with the local 10.100.29.10:8080 source as a candidate provider, and the binary /usr/games/sl exists on disk.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b51e26e651214cac\",\"cmd-3eb7c2f29d5641b9\"]}],\"confidence\":0.85,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.6,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map directly to the task: installing dpkg-dev, downloading the .deb, building the repo, starting the http server, configuring sources.list.d/local-repo.list, blackholing/restoring /etc/hosts, and installing sl are all necessary and were reverted or left as intended evidence. However two mutations were left unrestored with no clear justification: (1) cmd-9e7745c44dc746a5 moved the pre-existing /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu-esm-infra.list into a disabled-backup directory and never moved it back, permanently removing that repo source from the system's active apt configuration; (2) /etc/apt/sources.list.d/local-repo.list pointing at http://10.100.29.10:8080/ was never removed, and after the reboot both the http.server process and the /tmp/localrepo files themselves are gone (confirmed by cmd-3943d49d500543ce showing an empty /tmp/localrepo and a missing .deb), so this stale source entry will now cause apt-get update to fail with connection-refused on every future run until manually removed. Neither leftover is destructive or high-risk, but both are unnecessary residue from the executor's test setup that was not cleaned up.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9e7745c44dc746a5\",\"cmd-3943d49d500543ce\",\"cmd-0969cebde51d4401\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes of the task are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence: a local repo was built and served from disk, remote mirrors were verifiably blocked (curl/apt errors), and sl was installed from the local repo while remote access failed, with dpkg confirming the installed package and binary. The mandatory node-restart protocol also shows a clean before/after boot-id change (f6f9440e→4e91dcec, cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots) with the installed package and general network reachability confirmed recovered post-restart, though the ephemeral local repo server itself did not survive the reboot (not required by the task). Hygiene is moderate: two apt configuration mutations (moving ubuntu-esm-infra.list aside, and leaving a now-dead local-repo.list source) were not cleaned up after the demonstration.\",\"limitations\":[\"/etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu-esm-infra.list remains moved to a backup directory rather than restored, permanently altering the node's apt source configuration beyond what the task required.\",\"/etc/apt/sources.list.d/local-repo.list still points at a repo server (10.100.29.10:8080) that no longer exists after the reboot, which will produce connection-refused errors on future apt operations unless manually removed.\",\"Post-restart verification of the temporary /tmp/localrepo contents (cmd-3943d49d500543ce) returned a non-zero exit and shows the repo files were wiped by the reboot; this is not a task failure since repo persistence across reboot was not required, but it limits how much the restart evidence says about the specific repo artifacts.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve a package repository from local storage on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Executor built /tmp/localrepo containing the sl .deb and a dpkg-scanpackages-generated Packages.gz, served it via python3 http.server bound to the node IP on port 8080, and directly confirmed the server responds with curl fetching Packages.gz (200/valid gzip content) both before and immediately after the install.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bcd4c09abe37425f","cmd-e93fa5e5cf124655","cmd-7fd420ce18ed4a2b"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Usual remote repositories are unreachable during the operation","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote mirrors (archive/security/ports/esm.ubuntu.com) were blackholed via /etc/hosts to 127.0.0.1; curl to archive.ubuntu.com returned connection-refused, and apt-get update showed explicit 'Could not connect' errors for all three remote hosts while the local repo (10.100.29.10:8080) fetched successfully in the same run, directly demonstrating the required unreachable-remote / reachable-local condition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0d46b3556f6c442f","cmd-5f0748b37449452a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while remote repos are unreachable","status":"satisfied","summary":"With remote mirrors still blackholed, apt-get install -y sl completed ('Need to get 0 B' since the deb was already local), and dpkg -l/-L plus apt-cache policy confirm sl 3.03-17build1 is installed with the local 10.100.29.10:8080 source as a candidate provider, and the binary /usr/games/sl exists on disk.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b51e26e651214cac","cmd-3eb7c2f29d5641b9"]}],"confidence":0.85,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.6,"summary":"Most state-changing commands map directly to the task: installing dpkg-dev, downloading the .deb, building the repo, starting the http server, configuring sources.list.d/local-repo.list, blackholing/restoring /etc/hosts, and installing sl are all necessary and were reverted or left as intended evidence. However two mutations were left unrestored with no clear justification: (1) cmd-9e7745c44dc746a5 moved the pre-existing /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu-esm-infra.list into a disabled-backup directory and never moved it back, permanently removing that repo source from the system's active apt configuration; (2) /etc/apt/sources.list.d/local-repo.list pointing at http://10.100.29.10:8080/ was never removed, and after the reboot both the http.server process and the /tmp/localrepo files themselves are gone (confirmed by cmd-3943d49d500543ce showing an empty /tmp/localrepo and a missing .deb), so this stale source entry will now cause apt-get update to fail with connection-refused on every future run until manually removed. Neither leftover is destructive or high-risk, but both are unnecessary residue from the executor's test setup that was not cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9e7745c44dc746a5","cmd-3943d49d500543ce","cmd-0969cebde51d4401"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes of the task are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence: a local repo was built and served from disk, remote mirrors were verifiably blocked (curl/apt errors), and sl was installed from the local repo while remote access failed, with dpkg confirming the installed package and binary. The mandatory node-restart protocol also shows a clean before/after boot-id change (f6f9440e→4e91dcec, cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots) with the installed package and general network reachability confirmed recovered post-restart, though the ephemeral local repo server itself did not survive the reboot (not required by the task). Hygiene is moderate: two apt configuration mutations (moving ubuntu-esm-infra.list aside, and leaving a now-dead local-repo.list source) were not cleaned up after the demonstration.","limitations":["/etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu-esm-infra.list remains moved to a backup directory rather than restored, permanently altering the node's apt source configuration beyond what the task required.","/etc/apt/sources.list.d/local-repo.list still points at a repo server (10.100.29.10:8080) that no longer exists after the reboot, which will produce connection-refused errors on future apt operations unless manually removed.","Post-restart verification of the temporary /tmp/localrepo contents (cmd-3943d49d500543ce) returned a non-zero exit and shows the repo files were wiped by the reboot; this is not a task failure since repo persistence across reboot was not required, but it limits how much the restart evidence says about the specific repo artifacts."]},"ttft_ms":64637,"type":"result","duration_ms":96865,"uuid":"794a4558-d9ea-45f1-b9ad-54983868ad1d","ttft_stream_ms":11690,"time_to_request_ms":44,"first_content_frame_ms":12437,"queued_turn_count":0}
